# Demo seed — always restore local demo data

Local Postgres often loses data (compose recreate, volume wipe, fresh migrate). When that happens, **do not ask the user to re-login into a missing account** — restore the demo seed yourself.

## When to run it

Run seed **immediately** if any of these are true:

- Login fails for `demo@wealthos.test`
- DB has 0 users / empty org
- After `docker compose up`, volume recreate, or `alembic upgrade head` on an empty DB
- User says data “se borró”, “no puedo entrar”, “no hay demo”
- Starting a session where you will exercise the app UI against local stack

## Command (from repo root)

```bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
cd backend
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run python scripts/seed_demo.py --with-sample-data
```

Use `required_permissions: ["all"]` if Docker/DB access is sandboxed.

